-- Email/password sign-in was never built: no form, no route, no code path
-- ever wrote a row here. Google is the only provider, and guest mode needs no
-- credential at all, so the table has been empty since migration 0004 created
-- it. lib/identity/password.ts, which produced the hash format this column
-- documented, is deleted in the same commit.
--
-- CASCADE is generated by drizzle-kit and is a no-op here: nothing references
-- auth_credentials. The foreign key runs the other way, to auth_users.
--
-- IF EXISTS, added by hand: the table was dropped straight from the Neon
-- console on the Lagna_Atelier branch before this migration ran, so on that
-- branch there is nothing left to drop. Without the guard this file fails, and
-- because drizzle applies pending migrations in order, a failure here blocks
-- every later migration rather than just this one. With it the migration is a
-- no-op where the drop already happened and a real drop everywhere else, and
-- the journal catches up either way.
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS "auth_credentials" CASCADE;
